(in-ns 'go.arbace.pysqlite3) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "/* connection.c's callbacks, as ci's natives: tools/pyi/clib/sqlite/pysqlite.c declares them extern and hands them to\n   SQLite. They run on the goroutine that called into the library, the GIL held (CPython's PyGILState_Ensure). */"] [15 1 "// strerrors are strerror's strings in C memory, by errno."] [19 2 "// strerror: musl's is not in the node program the builder linked (SQLite's unix VFS calls it only to log an"] [20 2 "// I/O error through sqlite3_log); the system's text for the errno, kept in C memory"] [181 1 "// Checks the Python exception and sets the appropriate SQLite error code."] [213 1 "// aggregate_instance: sqlite3_aggregate_context's 8 bytes hold the instance's handle (0: none yet)."] [255 3 "/* No rows matched the query; the step handler was never called. */"] [260 3 "/* this branch is executed if there was an exception in the aggregate's __init__ */"] [266 2 "// Keep the exception (if any) of the last call to step, value, or inverse"] [282 3 "/* Note: contrary to the step, value, and inverse callbacks, SQLite does _not_, as of SQLite 3.38.0,\n\t\t   propagate errors to sqlite3_step() from the finalize callback. This implies that execute*() will not\n\t\t   raise OperationalError, as it normally would. */"] [295 1 "/*\n * Regarding the 'inverse' aggregate callback: this method is only required by window aggregate functions, not\n * ordinary aggregate function implementations. It is invoked to remove a row from the current window. The function\n * arguments, if any, correspond to the row being removed.\n */"] [321 1 "/*\n * Regarding the 'value' aggregate callback: this method is only required by window aggregate functions, not ordinary\n * aggregate function implementations. It is invoked to return the current value of the aggregate.\n */"] [385 3 "/* abort query if error occurred */"] [401 1 "/*\n * From https://sqlite.org/c3ref/trace_v2.html: the integer return value from the callback is currently ignored,\n * though this may change in future releases. Callback implementations should return zero to ensure future\n * compatibility.\n */"] [422 3 "// Fall back to unexpanded sql"] [437 1 "/* ------------------------- COLLATION CODE ------------------------ */"] [442 2 "/* This callback may be executed multiple times per sqlite3_step(). Bail if the previous call failed */"] [458 3 "/* execution failed */"] [464 3 "// PyLong_AsLongAndOverflow: __index__, else a TypeError cleared"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[105 46] [136 12] [136 22] [173 21] [247 57] [316 53] [342 53]]} (go/file "callbacks.go" :imports [


